Subject: shards api-run: an image run's run host takes shares another server serves (D286, image channel 52)
Why: the run host's side of Shards' D286, whose API side is change 0001-shards-api-shards-ipc-an-image-run-takes-shares-another (Hex's too): it takes the served shares' streams with the run's request (Unix: the links socket's SERVED_SHARES; Windows: the handles duplicated into it), puts each in a share slot after the run's own (hosted::served_slots), mounts it as a bind's, and saves no run holding one; kiln's microVM engine shares each agent's slates volume into its guest so (kiln goal 01a1ec34599974448f6b7663ddb07001). Upstream on Shards' branch agents/g265-kiln-shards-microvm-served-image-share (4ff40fc99 and 5376b406a on main 4776b2e56; e4e0118c8 and 74d1bc82f on 04481e36b), which ROOT lands after Shards' v0.8.0 tag; dropped once kiln takes a Shards revision holding it
Kiln-only: crates/shards, the binary kiln carries (ci/shards/pack.sh), which Hex's API-only copy of Shards doesn't take, so no product holds this change

